FLOW YOKE R3 — interpretation of the supplied STEP solids

INPUT  guide = A or B; manufacturing state = stock or finished
FRAME  origin on P2, X towards the rod, Z upwards; units are millimetres

SELECT the yoke for the matching guide.
KEEP the two feet, central pivot seat and rod axis in their guide-specific positions.
FORM a continuous arch between the feet.
EXTEND the magnet arm from a broad, shallow shoulder following the arch.
NARROW the arm towards the split rod boss and blend both ends.
ADD two local ears for the transverse clamp screw.

IF state = stock:
    retain machining pads on the mating faces
    keep the clamp and the centre of the pivot seat solid
    use a pilot through the rod boss
ELSE IF state = finished:
    use the nominal mating faces, seat recess and rod bore
    separate the ears with a slot opening into the bore
    provide clearance in the head-side ear and a tap pilot in the opposite ear

RETURN one solid. The matching finished STEP supplies the exact surface geometry.
